<title>USA: Compaq to sell pc's for under $1,000 - NYT.</title>
<headline>Compaq to sell pc's for under $1,000 - NYT.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-02-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Compaq Computer Corp plans to announce today that it will sell a personal computer priced less than $1,000, the New York Times reported Thursday.</p>
<p>The paper said Compaq's new personal computers will use a new chip produced by Cyrix, which contends that the chip offers similar performance as comparable-speed Pentium chips made by Intel, though the chips are not Pentium-equivalent.</p>
<p>The new machines are being made in Austin, Texas, by Taiwan's First International Computer.</p>
<p>((-- New York newsdesk 212-859-1610))</p>
</text>
